{"id":"13ac2c29-6cec-4781-8db3-d2c9065ee233","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"e35b707c7585ec53","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shared/fs-caller.ts","baseline":{"blob":"388e4eacf562682c4ea1306016b015feea62b774","start":1,"end":154},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","state","=","(","(","globalThis","as","Record","<","symbol",",","unknown",">",")","[","Symbol",".","for","(","\"","editor.fs-caller","\"",")","]","??=","{","\"","current","\"",":","undefined","}",")","as","{","\"","current","\"",":","string","|","undefined","}"]},"context":{"after":"4c5c7528e159a264"}},"payload":{"text":"Who is calling the workspace's store right now, for its counts (fs-boundaries.ts) and the architecture reports\n(architecture-zenfs.ts): a caller names itself for the length of each call it makes (`asCaller`), or hands a library\nan fs that does (`callerFs`: isomorphic-git's, `git`). zen-fs reaches its store synchronously from the call, so the\nname is the one set when the store's operation runs; a call that names nobody is a direct one.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T16:54:05.388Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T16:54:05.388Z"}
{"id":"293ff901-388d-4fc5-9d9f-a8b6932eb40f","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"fc732861b93d6aa4","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shared/fs-caller.ts","baseline":{"blob":"806add1f6289c8608fe893ea27c0390f2ba810b7","start":1135,"end":2304},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","function","callerFs","<","T","extends","object",">","(","fs",":","T",",","name",":","string",")",":","T","{","const","named","=","<","U","extends","object",">","(","target",":","U",")",":","U","=>","new","Proxy","(","target",",","{","\"","get","\"",":","(","object",",","property",",","receiver",")","=>","{","const","value","=","Reflect",".","get","(","object",",","property",",","receiver",")","as","unknown",";","return","typeof","value","===","\"","function","\"","?","(","...","args",":","unknown","[]",")","=>","asCaller","(","name",",","(",")","=>","(","value","as","(","...","parameters",":","unknown","[]",")","=>","unknown",")",".","apply","(","object",",","args",")",")",":","value",";","}","}",")",";","const","{","promises","}","=","fs","as","{","\"","promises","\"","?",":","object","}",";","const","twinned","=","promises","===","undefined","?","undefined",":","new","Proxy","(","promises",",","{","\"","get","\"",":","(","object",",","property",",","receiver",")","=>","{","const","twin","=","typeof","property","===","\"","string","\"","?","(","fs","as","Record","<","string",",","unknown",">",")","[","property","+","\"","Sync","\"","]",":","undefined",";","if","(","typeof","twin","===","\"","function","\"",")","{","return","async","(","...","args",":","unknown","[]",")","=>","asCaller","(","name",",","(",")","=>","(","twin","as","(","...","parameters",":","unknown","[]",")","=>","unknown",")",".","apply","(","fs",",","args",")",")",";","}","return","Reflect",".","get","(","named","(","object",")",",","property",",","receiver",")",";","}","}",")",";","return","new","Proxy","(","fs",",","{","\"","get","\"",":","(","object",",","property",",","receiver",")","=>","{","if","(","property","===","\"","promises","\"","&&","twinned","!==","undefined",")","{","return","twinned",";","}","return","Reflect",".","get","(","named","(","object",")",",","property",",","receiver",")",";","}","}",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"6c8e6bbd12efd552","after":"a1f577d7dcd073a6"}},"payload":{"text":"`fs` (a node-style fs, its `promises` too) whose every call is `name`'s. A promise call is answered by its synchronous\ntwin (`promises.stat` by `statSync`) where `fs` has one: zen-fs's promise functions await before they reach the store,\npast where the name holds — its store is in memory, so the twin costs the thread no more.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T16:54:02.313Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T16:54:02.313Z"}
